<title>COMOROS: Comoros air authority grounds local air fleet.</title>
<headline>Comoros air authority grounds local air fleet.</headline>
<dateline>MORONI 1997-04-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The civil aviation authority for the Comoros has grounded three Russian-made planes which make up the entire fleet of two private airlines operating in the Indian Ocean island republic, Comoros radio said.</p>
<p>The radio said on Saturday that the order was issued after the government ordered an inspection of the planes by an insurance and surveillance authority based in Reunion island, which is part of France.</p>
<p>The order covered two Yak-40's and an Antonov, which had been leased by the two small airlines.</p>
<p>Civil aviation director Abdallah Dada was quoted as saying the planes would not be allowed to carry passengers on internal flights within the Comoros.</p>
</text>
